{"1-3":{"people":[{"id":"asaph-h0623g","name":"Asaph","kind":"person","brief":"Returned musician","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"joseph-h3130g","name":"Joseph","kind":"person","brief":"Jacob's son","count":1,"firstVerse":1},{"id":"benjamin-h1144g","name":"Benjamin","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Israel","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"ephraim-h0669g","name":"Ephraim","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":2},{"id":"manasseh-h4519g","name":"Manasseh","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Joseph","count":1,"firstVerse":2}],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H3313","lemma":"יָפַע","tr":"ya·pah","gloss":"to shine","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H5090","lemma":"נָהַג","tr":"na·hag","gloss":"to lead","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":31},{"base":"H0238","lemma":"אָזַן","tr":"a·zan","gloss":"to listen","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":41},{"base":"H0215","lemma":"אוֹר","tr":"or","gloss":"to light","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43},{"base":"H1369","lemma":"גְּבוּרָה","tr":"ge·vu·rah","gloss":"might","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":61},{"base":"H3444","lemma":"יְשׁוּעָה","tr":"ye·shu·ah","gloss":"salvation","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":78},{"base":"H5782","lemma":"עוּר","tr":"ur","gloss":"to rouse","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":80},{"base":"H3742","lemma":"כְּרוּב","tr":"ke·ruv","gloss":"cherub","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":91},{"base":"H4519","lemma":"מְנַשֶּׁה","tr":"me·nash·sheh","gloss":"Manasseh","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":146},{"base":"H1144","lemma":"בִּנְיָמִין","tr":"bin·ya·min","gloss":"Benjamin","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":166}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"LAM","chapter":5,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":11,"source":"both","text":"Restore us to Yourself, O LORD, so we may return; renew our days as of old,","from":3},{"book":"NUM","chapter":6,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"may the LORD cause His face to shine upon you and be gracious to you;","from":3},{"book":"NUM","chapter":6,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":9,"source":"openbible","text":"may the LORD lift up His countenance toward you and give you peace.’","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":85,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Restore us, O God of our salvation, and put away Your displeasure toward us.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":4,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Many ask, “Who can show us the good?” Shine the light of Your face upon us, O LORD.","from":3},{"book":"PSA","chapter":35,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Awake and rise to my defense, to my cause, my God and my Lord!","from":2},{"book":"PSA","chapter":50,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"From Zion, perfect in beauty, God shines forth.","from":1},{"book":"PSA","chapter":77,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"You led Your people like a flock by the hand of Moses and Aaron.","from":1}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":3}]},"4-7":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H1832","lemma":"דִּמְעָה","tr":"dim·ah","gloss":"tears","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23},{"base":"H6635","lemma":"צָבָא","tr":"tsa·va","gloss":"army","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":484},{"base":"H6225","lemma":"עָשַׁן","tr":"a·shan","gloss":"be angry","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H4066","lemma":"מָדוֹן","tr":"ma·don","gloss":"strife","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":10},{"base":"H3932","lemma":"לָעַג","tr":"la·ag","gloss":"to mock","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":18},{"base":"H7934","lemma":"שָׁכֵן","tr":"sha·khen","gloss":"neighboring","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H7991","lemma":"שָׁלִישׁ","tr":"sha·lish","gloss":"third","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":20},{"base":"H0215","lemma":"אוֹר","tr":"or","gloss":"to light","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43},{"base":"H4970","lemma":"מָתַי","tr":"ma·tay","gloss":"how","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43},{"base":"H8248","lemma":"שָׁקָה","tr":"sha·qah","gloss":"to water: watering","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":61}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":42,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"My tears have been my food both day and night, while men ask me all day long, “Where is your God?”","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":30,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"The Lord will give you the bread of adversity and the water of affliction, but your Teacher will no longer hide Himself—with your own eyes you will see Him.","from":5},{"book":"PSA","chapter":51,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me.","from":7},{"book":"PSA","chapter":102,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"For I have eaten ashes like bread and mixed my drink with tears","from":5},{"book":"ISA","chapter":64,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"You welcome those who gladly do right, who remember Your ways. Surely You were angry, for we sinned. How can we be saved if we remain in our sins?","from":7},{"book":"DEU","chapter":29,"verse":20,"verseEnd":20,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The LORD will never be willing to forgive him. Instead, His anger and jealousy will burn against that man, and every curse written in this book will fall upon him. The LORD will blot out his name from under heaven","from":4},{"book":"JDG","chapter":16,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And while their hearts were merry, they said, “Call for Samson to entertain us.” So they called Samson out of the prison to entertain them. And they stationed him between the pillars.","from":6},{"book":"JOB","chapter":6,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"My soul refuses to touch them; they are loathsome food to me.","from":5}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"8-13":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"egypt-h4714g","name":"Egypt","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":8},{"id":"euphrates-h6578","name":"Euphrates","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":11}],"words":[{"base":"H0717","lemma":"אָרָה","tr":"a·rah","gloss":"to pluck","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H2123","lemma":"זִיז","tr":"ziz","gloss":"creature","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":3},{"base":"H3127","lemma":"יוֹנֶ֫קֶת","tr":"yo·ne·qet","gloss":"shoot","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":6},{"base":"H2386","lemma":"חֲזִיר","tr":"cha·zir","gloss":"swine","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H6057","lemma":"עָנָף","tr":"a·naph","gloss":"branch","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":7},{"base":"H8327","lemma":"שָׁרַשׁ","tr":"sha·rash","gloss":"to uproot","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":8},{"base":"H1447","lemma":"גָּדֵר","tr":"ga·der","gloss":"wall","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":12},{"base":"H8328","lemma":"שֹׁ֫רֶשׁ","tr":"she·resh","gloss":"root","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":33},{"base":"H1644","lemma":"גָּרַשׁ","tr":"ga·rash","gloss":"to drive out: drive out","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":47},{"base":"H6555","lemma":"פָּרַץ","tr":"pa·rats","gloss":"to break through","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":48}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"PSA","chapter":44,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"With Your hand You drove out the nations and planted our fathers there; You crushed the peoples and cast them out.","from":8},{"book":"ISA","chapter":5,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Now I will tell you what I am about to do to My vineyard: I will take away its hedge, and it will be consumed; I will tear down its wall, and it will be trampled.","from":12},{"book":"JER","chapter":2,"verse":21,"verseEnd":21,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"I had planted you like a choice vine from the very best seed. How could you turn yourself before Me into a rotten, wild vine?","from":8},{"book":"JER","chapter":12,"verse":10,"verseEnd":10,"votes":6,"source":"openbible","text":"Many shepherds have destroyed My vineyard; they have trampled My plot of ground. They have turned My pleasant field into a desolate wasteland.","from":8},{"book":"EZK","chapter":17,"verse":6,"verseEnd":6,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"It sprouted and became a spreading vine, low in height, with branches turned toward him; yet its roots remained where it stood. So it became a vine and yielded branches and sent out shoots.","from":8},{"book":"PSA","chapter":72,"verse":8,"verseEnd":8,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"May he rule from sea to sea, and from the Euphrates to the ends of the earth.","from":11},{"book":"ISA","chapter":5,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"I will sing for my beloved a song of his vineyard: My beloved had a vineyard on a very fertile hill.","from":8},{"book":"ISA","chapter":5,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"For the vineyard of the LORD of Hosts is the house of Israel, and the men of Judah are the plant of His delight. He looked for justice, but saw bloodshed; for righteousness, but heard a cry of distress.","from":8}],"notes":[{"id":"isa-5-vine-john-15","title":"Israel the vine and Jesus the true vine","kind":"type"}],"groups":[]},"14-19":{"people":[],"places":[],"words":[{"base":"H0553","lemma":"אָמֵץ","tr":"a·mats","gloss":"to strengthen","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":41},{"base":"H3225","lemma":"יָמִין","tr":"ya·min","gloss":"right","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":140},{"base":"H9032","lemma":"ךְ","tr":"kh","gloss":"you","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":333},{"base":"H3683","lemma":"כָּסַח","tr":"ka·sach","gloss":"to cut","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6635","lemma":"צָבָא","tr":"tsa·va","gloss":"army","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":484},{"base":"H5472","lemma":"סוּג","tr":"sug","gloss":"to turn","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":14},{"base":"H1606","lemma":"גְּעָרָה","tr":"ge·a·rah","gloss":"rebuke","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":15},{"base":"H7725","lemma":"שׁוּב","tr":"shuv","gloss":"to return: return","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":1057},{"base":"H0215","lemma":"אוֹר","tr":"or","gloss":"to light","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":43},{"base":"H1612","lemma":"גֶּ֫פֶן","tr":"ge·phen","gloss":"vine","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":55}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":63,"verse":15,"verseEnd":15,"votes":8,"source":"both","text":"Look down from heaven and see, from Your holy and glorious habitation. Where are Your zeal and might? Your yearning and compassion for me are restrained.","from":14},{"book":"PSA","chapter":39,"verse":11,"verseEnd":11,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"You discipline and correct a man for his iniquity, consuming like a moth what he holds dear; surely each man is but a vapor. Selah","from":16},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":25,"verseEnd":25,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"My soul cleaves to the dust; revive me according to Your word.","from":18},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":40,"verseEnd":40,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"How I long for Your precepts! Revive me in Your righteousness.","from":18},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":107,"verseEnd":107,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I am severely afflicted, O LORD; revive me through Your word.","from":18},{"book":"PSA","chapter":119,"verse":154,"verseEnd":154,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Defend my cause and redeem me; revive me according to Your word.","from":18},{"book":"JER","chapter":3,"verse":22,"verseEnd":22,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"“Return, O faithless children, and I will heal your faithlessness.” “Here we are. We come to You, for You are the LORD our God.","from":19},{"book":"JER","chapter":3,"verse":23,"verseEnd":23,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Surely deception comes from the hills, and commotion from the mountains. Surely the salvation of Israel is in the LORD our God.","from":19}],"notes":[{"id":"isa-5-vine-john-15","title":"Israel the vine and Jesus the true vine","kind":"type"}],"groups":[]}}